    {
      "id": "6grka79",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Motion"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Motion describes a change in an object's position over time relative to a fixed frame of reference.",
        "Distance measures total path length (scalar), whereas displacement measures the shortest straight line between initial and final points (vector).",
        "Speed is the rate of distance covered, while velocity includes both speed and direction of motion.",
        "Acceleration represents the rate of change of velocity over time.",
        "Equations of motion mathematically describe uniform acceleration in a straight line."
      ],
      "id": "8w7tzuj"
    },
