    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Displacement can be zero even when distance is positive (e.g., completing a full circular lap).",
        "The slope of a Distance-Time graph gives Speed, whereas the slope of a Velocity-Time graph gives Acceleration.",
        "The area under a Velocity-Time graph equals the total Displacement covered by the body.",
        "Equations of motion apply only when acceleration is uniform/constant."
      ],
      "id": "7brn6ei"
